    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0500" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW 1939/2088</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-30">December 30, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to the last paragraph, numbered 4, of the British memorandum containing
                    the text of telegram dated December 25 from Mr. Eden, hereto attached,<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d260-f1"/> I informed Mr. Michael Wright, Secretary<anchor
                        n="22" xml:id="d260-f2"/> of the British Embassy, that this Government was
                    fully in accord with the proposed reply to be made by the British Government to
                    the reported approach from German sources.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James Clement Dunn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
